From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josip Seketa <josip.seketa@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 04:35:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 66/66] gdb: do not hide a lost connection when inserting a
 momentary breakpoint

With target-non-stop on, a lost connection while inserting a step-resume breakpoint was dropped.

diff --git a/gdb/breakpoint.c b/gdb/breakpoint.c
index e6f36f3285c..5da705c1160 100644
--- a/gdb/breakpoint.c
+++ b/gdb/breakpoint.c
@@ -12119,6 +12119,10 @@ update_global_location_list_nothrow (enum ugll_insert_mode insert_mode)
     }
   catch (const gdb_exception_error &e)
     {
+      /* A breakpoint that cannot be inserted now is reported when the
+	 program is resumed.  But a target that has gone cannot be
+	 resumed: the caller must know.  */
+      rethrow_on_target_close_error (e);
     }
 }
 
